  description: "M15D § Acceptance scenario 4 — 'H2 + O2 mix flashes at stoichiometric ratio when sparked'. A sealed room with 100 kPa H2 + 50 kPa O2 (the 2:1 stoichiometric mix per 2 H2 + O2 -> 2 H2O) at 295 K. A spark source ignites; rxn.combustion.h2_o2 fires (delta_h=-483.6, autoignition at 700 K). The pressure spike is recorded in the atmos snapshot per the PV=nRT model in M19, and reaction_autoignited carries delta_h_kj = -483.6 * moles_reacted. The deafening radius around the spark fires the M16 hearing-damage event.",
